% ============================================================================
% joint-formed-by.query.adj — worked recall over the joint-formed-by library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what bones form the
% pivot joint?" (direct) or "which joint type does the trapezium help form?"
% (reverse) — it states no fact of its own — it only `import`s the grounded
% table and asks binding queries. A joint type not tabled here abstains
% honestly — the engine never invents a forming bone.
% ============================================================================

import "joint-formed-by.adj"

? joint_formed_by(pivot, $Bone)          % expect atlas, then axis
? joint_formed_by($Type, trapezium)       % reverse bind — expect saddle
? joint_formed_by(hinge, $Bone)            % expect abstain -- a real, already-tabled joint type, but its own quote names only an example joint, never the specific forming bones
